    LIST `annex א'8 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'9 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'10 of 1.9.2016`

`the 2015 annexes of menahalim-sganim-chadashim` MEANS
    LIST `annex א of 2015`, `annex ב of 2015`, `annex ג of 2015`

§§ `בדיקת הטבלאות`

-- (1) The rows: the complexity levels the 2015 table prints (levels 1 to 8; a deputy's from 2), the
-- grades א to ד.
#ASSERT and (zipWith (GIVEN t, a YIELD `the published labels of` t EQUALS catMaybes (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `row label`) (`the rows of the 2015 annex` a)))
                     `the tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim` `the 2015 annexes of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN t YIELD t's `published table from` EQUALS `the managers' tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim are updated from`) `the tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`

-- (2) The 2015 tables raised to 1.1.2015: each cell taken back by the rise
-- of 1.1.2015 over the third part's tables (1.0635/1.0575, as the tables of
-- 1.1.2015 rise) is the 2015 table's cell to the nearest shekel
-- (convention rounding.half). A check sets the 2015 cell beside the cell
-- here taken back and rounded.
GIVEN t IS A `published table`, a IS A `2015 salary annex`
GIVETH A LIST OF `published cell check`
DECIDE `the cells of menahalim-sganim-chadashim taken back to 2015 beside` t a IS
    concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD
                     concat (map (GIVEN c YIELD
                                      CONSIDER `the 2015 table pay` a (r's `published row label`) (c's grade)
                                      WHEN JUST old THEN LIST (`a published check` (r's `published row label`) (c's grade) old
                                                                   (`to the nearest whole` (c's pay DIVIDED BY `the rise of 1.1.2015 over the third part's tables`)))
                                      WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY)
                                 (r's `published row cells`)))
                (t's `published table rows`))

`the 2015 checks of menahalim-sganim-chadashim` MEANS
    concat (zipWith `the cells of menahalim-sganim-chadashim taken back to 2015 beside` `the tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim` `the 2015 annexes of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`)

#ASSERT count `the 2015 checks of menahalim-sganim-chadashim` EQUALS sum (map `the published cell count of` `the tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`)
#ASSERT null (`the published misses in` `the 2015 checks of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`)

-- The new principals' and deputies' tables are the existing ones without
-- their intermediate grades, as the 2015 agreement's own are: every cell of
-- א'8, א'9 and א'10 is the cell of א'11, א'15 and א'19 (imported) at the same
-- level and grade.
#ASSERT and (zipWith (GIVEN new, old YIELD null (`the published misses in` (`the published cells beside` (`the same published cell of` old) `in` new))
                                     AND `the published cells no rule reaches` (`the same published cell of` old) `in` new EQUALS 0)
                     `the tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`
                     (LIST `annex א'11 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'15 of 1.9.2016`, `annex א'19 of 1.9.2016`))

-- (3) Every table rises along its grades and down its levels, so "the
-- grade nearest at or above" (§71(ב)) is one cell.
#ASSERT all `the published table rises along its grades and down its rows` `the tables of menahalim-sganim-chadashim`

-- The tables at work.
#ASSERT `the published table pay on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2016) `annex א'8 of 1.9.2016` 1 1 EQUALS JUST 14032.14
